{"title":"Career roadmap — Cultural Officer","role":"Cultural Officer","summary":"A Cultural Officer works on the preservation, promotion and administration of cultural heritage, traditions, arts, literature, festivals, museums, cultural programmes and knowledge systems. With a background in Vedic Studies, Indology, Yoga Philosophy or Jyotisha, the strongest career profile combines Indian knowledge systems + heritage management + research + cultural administration + digital communication.","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Course":"Vedic Studies / Indology / Yoga Philosophy / Jyotisha"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build expertise in Indian culture, heritage, Sanskrit/Indic sources, cultural documentation, event coordination and research"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Work in cultural institutions, museums, universities, NGOs, government cultural departments, foundations or international cultural organisations"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Move into Cultural Programme Management, Heritage Management, Cultural Diplomacy or Institutional Cultural Strategy"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Lead major cultural institutions, international cultural programmes, heritage initiatives, museums, cultural foundations or knowledge-preservation projects"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Cultural and historical foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Indian history and civilisation"},{"text":"Indian art and architecture"},{"text":"Vedic and post-Vedic traditions"},{"text":"Indian philosophy"},{"text":"Sanskrit/Indic terminology"},{"text":"Indian literature"},{"text":"Major cultural institutions and heritage sites"},{"text":"Cultural anthropology"},{"text":"Basics of archaeology